# Check text out with LF on every platform. winlab's shell scripts run in
# Linux guests and much of its text is written into guests or compared byte
# for byte; a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf (the GitHub runner's and
# Git for Windows' default) would turn content/agent/fabric-agent.sh and the
# roles into CRLF, which sh in the guest cannot run, and the exe is built
# from that checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Batch files keep the platform's line ends (CRLF on Windows), as cmd.exe wants.
*.cmd text=auto !eol
